# {{ClassName}}

A VS Code extension scaffold for the **{{ClassName}}** DSL, generated by `unlaxer init`.

This project bundles:

- a Java-based **LSP server** generated from `grammar/{{name}}.ubnf`
- {{#dap}}a **DAP (Debug Adapter Protocol)** server for step-through debugging
- {{/dap}}{{^dap}}*(DAP debugging is **not** included — re-run `unlaxer init` with `--with-dap` if you want it)*
- {{/dap}}a **VS Code extension** that ships the fat jar inside the VSIX

> 日本語版: [README.ja.md](README.ja.md)

## Quick start (10 minutes)

```bash
# 1. build everything (codegen → fat jar → npm install → vsix)
make all

# 2. install the produced VSIX into your local VS Code
make install-vsix

# 3. open any file with the {{extension}} extension
```

## Project layout

```
{{name}}/
├── grammar/{{name}}.ubnf            # your DSL definition (edit this!)
├── pom.xml                            # Maven build (codegen + fat jar + vsix)
├── Makefile                           # convenience targets
├── vscode-extension/
│   ├── package.json
│   ├── language-configuration.json
│   ├── tsconfig.json
│   ├── syntaxes/{{name}}.tmLanguage.json   # auto-generated, regenerate via codegen
│   ├── src/extension.ts
│   └── server-dist/                  # fat jar lands here at `mvn package`
├── IMPLEMENTATION.md                  # **how to extend / customize**
├── IMPLEMENTATION.ja.md               # 日本語版実装ガイド
└── README.md / README.ja.md
```

